# Fixtures are byte-exact filter inputs; eol conversion must never touch them.
# Without this, Windows runners (core.autocrlf=true) check fixtures out with
# CRLF, and tests that synthesize CRLF input from them produce \r\r\n.
tests/fixtures/** -text

# CHANGELOG.md diverges permanently: the fork keeps its own -dev-fork sections that upstream
# never has. union merge keeps BOTH sides' lines on conflict so a fork sync neither drops the
# fork's authored history nor upstream's new entries. (Spec: rtk-upgrade/SKILL.md § Versioning.)
CHANGELOG.md merge=union

# ── Enterprise distribution surface (export-ignore) ───────────────────────────
# scripts/export-enterprise.sh step 1 is `git archive <ref> | tar -x`, which emits EVERY tracked
# path. Until 2026-07-24 nothing bounded that, so the published distro shipped the fork's internal
# engineering context to customers — agent tooling, internal instructions, and FORK_NOTES.md, a
# running log of this fork's security posture, its known gaps and its unfixed defects.
#
# `export-ignore` makes the shipped surface an explicit, reviewable declaration instead of
# "whatever happens to be tracked". This is deliberately preferred over scrubbing: an allowlist in
# the residual scan has to be maintained per-pattern forever, while an exclusion removes whole
# classes of leak permanently and is auditable at a glance.
#
# DRIFT GUARD: adding a fork-internal file at the repo root, or a new directory of fork tooling,
# means adding it here. Anything NOT listed here ships to customers. Verify after any change with:
#   git archive harden/no-egress | tar -t | awk -F/ '{print ($1 ~ /\./ ? $1 : $1"/")}' | sort -u
.claude/                            export-ignore
.github/                            export-ignore
scripts/                            export-ignore
AGENTS.md                           export-ignore
CLAUDE.md                           export-ignore
FORK_NOTES.md                       export-ignore
UPSTREAM_CANDIDATES.md              export-ignore
docs/maintainers/                   export-ignore

# The telemetry surface itself. The dev fork legitimately documents telemetry (it is a real,
# feature-gated capability here); the distro must not, because the distro has no telemetry at all.
# Keeping these out of `git archive` is what stops the shipped docs contradicting the shipped code.
docs/TELEMETRY.md                   export-ignore
docs/guide/resources/telemetry.md   export-ignore
